        <h2>2. Acceptance of These Terms</h2>
        <p>By accessing this website or enrolling in any of the mentorship plans described below, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, please do not use our Services.</p>

        <h2>3. Description of Services</h2>
        <p>We offer three subscription plans, each billed on a recurring 4-week cycle. All plans include a personalized study roadmap (built with you at the very start), unlimited access to our custom kanji and vocabulary app with spaced repetition, and JLPT-focused practice materials. Beyond that shared foundation, the plans differ as follows:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Async Mentorship</strong> — a fully asynchronous plan with no recurring live sessions. It includes a one-time live roadmap call at the start of your enrollment, a new written theory-and-practice pack from your mentor every week, and personal async correction of your submitted exercises plus written answers to your questions about that week's material. There is no fixed weekly live call, no group, and no Certificate of Achievement (see Section 7) under this plan.</li>
          <li><strong>Full-Access Mentorship</strong> — includes four premium 60-minute live sessions per 4-week cycle, delivered in a small-group format of 3 students who share the same weekly time slot. Each student joins their own separate, private voice channel; the mentor moves between these channels in turn, spending part of the hour speaking directly and individually with each student. Students cannot hear the mentor's conversations with the other two students in their group, as these take place in different private channels. This is not a private one-on-one tutoring session: the 60-minute slot is shared between 3 students, so each student's individual speaking time with the mentor is a portion of that hour, in accordance with the Three-Pillar System described on our website. This plan includes a Certificate of Achievement (Section 7).</li>
          <li><strong>1-on-1 VIP Mentorship</strong> — includes four premium 60-minute live sessions per 4-week cycle, delivered 100% privately: your full hour with the mentor, one-on-one, not shared with any other student. This plan includes a Certificate of Achievement (Section 7).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may also offer a free, one-time 15-minute introductory call, as described in Section 4 below. This call is not part of, and does not require enrollment in, any subscription plan.</p>

        <h2>4. Free Introductory Call</h2>
        <p>Where offered on our website, the 15-minute introductory call is provided free of charge and does not require you to purchase or commit to any subscription plan. It is intended as a one-time opportunity per person to experience our teaching approach before enrolling. We reserve the right to decline or limit repeat requests for this free call. Any contact details you provide to schedule this call are processed in accordance with our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="highlight">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

        <h2>5. Enrollment and Payment</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Enrollment is completed by selecting one of the three subscription plans described in Section 3 and paying through our secure checkout page, operated by our payment processor, Stripe. Before you are asked to pay, the checkout page clearly displays the total price, currency, and billing frequency for your plan; you will also be asked to expressly accept these Terms before completing payment.</li>
          <li>Each plan is billed on a recurring 4-week cycle that renews automatically until cancelled. The price displayed to you may be adjusted automatically based on certain factors. These prices do not include VAT, as Kitsunebi Miyabi SRL is not a VAT payer ("neplătitoare de TVA") under Romanian law. Pricing is subject to change with reasonable notice for future billing cycles, in accordance with Section 15.</li>
          <li>You are charged, and your subscription renews, in the same currency that was displayed to you and shown at checkout for your plan.</li>
          <li>Payment is processed securely by Stripe. We do not collect or store your full card details; see our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="highlight">Privacy Policy</a> for details on how payment data is handled.</li>
          <li>By completing a subscription purchase, you authorize us to charge your chosen payment method every 4 weeks until you cancel in accordance with Section 6. Immediately after each successful payment, you will receive a confirmation by email containing your plan, the price and currency charged, your billing cycle, and a summary of your cancellation and withdrawal rights, together with a secure link where you can view your billing details at any time.</li>
          <li>Access to the plan's live sessions (if any), the personalized roadmap, and the vocab app for a given cycle is conditional on payment for that cycle being received.</li>
          <li>You may switch between plans effective from your next billing cycle by contacting us at <strong class="highlight text-red-300">vici.sensei@gmail.com</strong>; a plan change does not restart or extend your current cycle.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Cancellation and Right of Withdrawal</h2>
        <p>You may cancel your subscription, on any plan, at any time by contacting us at <strong class="highlight text-red-300">vici.sensei@gmail.com</strong>. Cancelling stops future renewals only: regardless of when you cancel, you retain full access to the current 4-week cycle you have already paid for, and your payment method will not be charged again after that. Cancellation does not entitle you to a refund for the current cycle or any previous cycle. This no-refund policy is subject to the narrow statutory exception described below.</p>
        <p>If you are a consumer entering into this contract at a distance, Romanian law (GEO no. 34/2014) grants you a 14-calendar-day right to withdraw from the contract without giving any reason. This right applies to services as well as goods, but because our Services begin immediately upon enrollment, it applies differently than it would for a physical product: by checking the box to accept these Terms and completing payment, you expressly request that we begin performing the Services immediately, and you acknowledge that you progressively lose this right as the Services are delivered during your first cycle, as follows:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Full-Access and VIP plans:</strong> you lose the right of withdrawal session by session, as each live session in your first cycle is fully delivered.</li>
          <li><strong>Async plan:</strong> you lose the right of withdrawal pack by pack, as each weekly theory-and-practice pack in your first cycle is delivered to you.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you formally exercise this statutory right of withdrawal within 14 calendar days of your first enrollment, before all sessions or packs (as applicable to your plan) in your first cycle have been delivered, we will refund the portion of your first payment corresponding to what has not yet been delivered. This statutory right applies only to your first enrollment on a given plan — it does not reopen with each renewal — and any cancellation made outside this 14-day window, or after your first cycle, is governed solely by the no-refund policy above.</p>
        <p>You may exercise your right of withdrawal by contacting us at <strong class="highlight text-red-300">vici.sensei@gmail.com</strong>.</p>

        <h2>7. Certificate of Achievement</h2>
        <p>Students enrolled in the Full-Access or VIP plan receive a Certificate of Achievement upon request, reflecting the duration of their study with us and a JLPT-equivalent level. This certificate is our mentor's own personal assessment of your progress, based on the material covered together. It is not an official JLPT certification, is not issued or endorsed by the Japan Foundation or any JLPT-administering body, and is not a substitute for sitting and passing an official JLPT exam. The Async plan does not include a Certificate of Achievement.</p>

        <h2>8. Your Responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate contact and billing information;</li>
          <li>If enrolled in the Full-Access or VIP plan, attend your scheduled weekly live session at its fixed time. If enrolled in the Async plan, submit your weekly exercises and questions in a timely manner so they can be corrected and answered before your next pack is delivered;</li>
          <li>Ensure you have the equipment and internet connection necessary to join live sessions (if applicable to your plan) on the platform used to host them;</li>
          <li>Use the kanji and vocabulary app and all course materials for your own personal, non-commercial study only;</li>
          <li>If enrolled in the Full-Access plan, not disclose to anyone outside your group any personal information you learn about other participants during group sessions.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>9. Missed Live Sessions</h2>
        <p>This section applies only to the Full-Access and VIP plans, which include live sessions.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Full-Access plan:</strong> because sessions are delivered in a small-group format, a missed session can be rescheduled only if all members of your group unanimously agree to a new time. If that is not possible, we will do our best to accommodate you in another active group for that week. If no alternative slot is available, you will not fall behind: we will provide you with the complete learning materials and tasks that would have been covered during that session. No cash refund or account credit is given for a missed session.</li>
          <li><strong>VIP plan:</strong> because your sessions are 100% private, a missed session can be rescheduled directly with your mentor, subject to availability, without needing anyone else's agreement. If no alternative time can be arranged within the current cycle, we will provide you with the complete learning materials and tasks that would have been covered during that session. No cash refund or account credit is given for a missed session.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>10. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>All course materials, the study roadmap, the kanji and vocabulary app, and related content are the property of Kitsunebi Miyabi SRL or its licensors and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. You are granted a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use these materials for your own personal learning while enrolled in the program. You may not reproduce, redistribute, or resell any course materials without our prior written consent.</p>

        <h2>11. Third-Party Platforms</h2>
        <p>Live sessions and communications are conducted through third-party platforms such as Discord, WhatsApp, and Gmail. We are not responsible for the availability, security, or policies of these platforms, and your use of them is also subject to their own terms of service.</p>

        <h2>12. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Kitsunebi Miyabi SRL shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the Services. Our total liability for any claim arising from these Terms shall not exceed the amount you have paid for the current subscription cycle. Nothing in these Terms limits any liability that cannot be limited under applicable Romanian consumer protection law.</p>

        <h2>13. Force Majeure</h2>
        <p>Neither party shall be liable for any failure or delay in performing its obligations under these Terms where this results from circumstances beyond that party's reasonable control, including fires, natural disasters, war, internet or platform outages, or medical emergencies ("Force Majeure Event"). Where a Force Majeure Event prevents either party from starting, continuing, or completing the Services, either party may terminate the affected subscription without penalty. This section does not affect your statutory rights as a consumer.</p>

        <h2>14. Termination</h2>
        <p>We may suspend or terminate your access to the Services if you breach these Terms or fail to make payment for a subscription cycle. You may terminate your enrollment at any time in accordance with Section 6.</p>

        <h2>15. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these Terms, our plan structure, or subscription pricing from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page indicates when they were last revised.</p>
        <p>For minor or administrative changes that do not affect your rights or the price or nature of the Services you receive, the update takes effect immediately upon publication, and your continued use of the Services after that date constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.</p>
        <p>For changes affecting the price of your subscription, the frequency or format of live sessions, or your rights as a consumer, we will notify active subscribers by email at least 4 weeks before the change takes effect. If you do not agree with the change, you may cancel your subscription without penalty at any time before the change takes effect, in accordance with Section 6. Continued enrollment and payment after that 4-week notice period constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.</p>

        <h2>16. Complaints and Alternative Dispute Resolution</h2>
        <p>If you have a complaint, please contact us first at <strong class="highlight text-red-300">vici.sensei@gmail.com</strong> so we can try to resolve it directly. As a consumer, you are also entitled to use the Alternative Dispute Resolution (SAL) platform operated by the Romanian National Authority for Consumer Protection (ANPC), accessible at <a href="https://reclamatiisal.anpc.ro/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="highlight">reclamatiisal.anpc.ro</a>, as well as the European Commission's Online Dispute Resolution platform.</p>

        <h2>17. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>These Terms are governed by Romanian law. Any dispute that cannot be resolved amicably or through the SAL platform referenced above shall be submitted to the competent courts of Romania.</p>

